892.0,"Scam lords: BJP targets Siddaramaiah, DK Shivakumar in latest X post; case filed - India Today",India Today,"Fri, 30 Jan 2026 08:00:00 GMT",https://www.indiatoday.in/india/karnataka/story/siddaramaiah-dk-shivakumar-scam-lords-karnataka-bjp-x-post-congress-file-complaint-2860253-2026-01-30,success_decoder,success,"Scam lords: BJP targets Siddaramaiah, DK Shivakumar in latest X post; case filed",Sagay Raj,2026-01-30,"Scam lords: BJP targets Siddaramaiah, DK Shivakumar in latest X post; case filed
In a post on X, the Karnataka BJP shared an image of Chief Minister Siddaramaiah, DK Shivakumar and other cabinet ministers, accusing them of being involved in large-scale scams.
The Karnataka Pradesh Congress Committee (KPCC) has moved the cybercrime police against the BJP's Karnataka X handle, accusing it of posting ""defamatory content"" targeting Chief Minister Siddaramaiah, Deputy Chief Minister DK Shivakumar and other ministers.
The complaint was filed at the Cyber Crime Police Station in Bengaluru by the KPCC lawyers' team after a post surfaced using photographs of Siddaramaiah, Shivakumar and cabinet ministers with the caption ""scam lords"".
""This is the real story of the scam empire of the @INCKarnataka government that has been looting Karnataka day and night!!"" the post read.
In its submission, the Congress alleged the post amounted to character assassination and was designed to mislead the public and create confusion in society. The party said the accusations were malicious, unsubstantiated and aimed at tarnishing the reputation of elected representatives.
Police officials confirmed they have received the complaint, issued an acknowledgement and registered a case. ""Further investigation will be carried out to examine the allegations and determine whether there are legal violations,"" an officer said.
The legal action came amid a parallel political standoff over alleged irregularities in the state's excise department. Karnataka BJP president BY Vijayendra, earlier this week, demanded a high-level probe into what he described as a Rs 6,000 crore excise scam and called for the resignation of Excise Minister Ramappa Timmapur.
Vijayendra said the matter should be investigated either by a sitting High Court judge or the Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI).
""Proof has already emerged, but Chief Minister Siddaramaiah is not willing to discuss this on the floor of the House. Investigation by the CBI or a sitting High Court judge is the only answer. The Karnataka government is trying to cover up the scam. Outside and inside the House, we will demand the resignation of the excise minister,"" he told reporters in Bengaluru.
The political sparring between the BJP and Congress in the state has sharpened in recent days, with both sides trading barbs over multiple issues. Earlier, the BJP had circulated AI-generated videos on social media to target the Congress, highlighting the reported leadership tussle between Siddaramaiah and Shivakumar.",392,,True,False
896.0,Vigilance to unearth scam pertaining to installation of AI cameras across Kerala - Kerala Kaumudi,Kerala Kaumudi,"Thu, 27 Apr 2023 07:00:00 GMT",https://keralakaumudi.com/en/kerala/crime/vigilance-to-unearth-scam-pertaining-to-installation-of-ai-cameras-across-kerala-1055896,success_decoder,success,Vigilance to unearth scam pertaining to installation of AI cameras across Kerala,Keralakaumudi Daily,2023-04-27,"THIRUVANANTHAPURAM: Vigilance is probing the massive scam involving the installation of 726 artificial intelligence cameras at a cost of Rs 232.25 crore to detect traffic violations. They will investigate the manipulations made in the tender, sub-contracts and consultancy of the project, which aims to collect Rs 424 crores from the people as fine in five years.
Vigilance seized the files from Keltron and interrogated the three officers in charge. The officials have been directed to produce all documents immediately. Vigilance had found that there was substance in the complaint filed by the Indian Anti-Corruption Mission in Karunagapally last October.
Vigilance chief Manoj Abraham sought permission from the Chief Minister for the investigation as the camera was installed as per the government order. The complaint is against Rajeev Puthalath, who was the Joint Transport Commissioner, and the section clerk. Thiruvananthapuram's 1st Special Unit SP Reg Jacob's preliminary investigation will be completed within a month. An FIR will be registered if any irregularity is found.
