The Rajasthan Special Operations Group (SOG) has arrested Prince Saini, also known as Banshilal, along with two accomplices, for defrauding people of crores through fake companies. The main accused, Prince Saini, is alleged to have defrauded people of ₹50 crore over multiple incidents. He was caught before he could flee and will be presented in court for remand.
Prince Saini, a resident of Dhoru village in Bhopalgarh, Jodhpur, failed his 12th grade in 2017. He then started a fake company called Tronex World, collecting ₹12,000 each from 54 people through a chain system software business, absconding with ₹6.48 lakh. In 2022, he launched Grow More Education Private Limited, collecting annual fees of ₹3,000 from 2,200 students under the pretext of online coaching, swindling ₹66 lakh. Subsequently, he promised 96–120% annual returns under Groomer Education schemes.
Lured investors with luxury cars
Prince Saini later created Harvest AI Technology Private Limited, claiming that investors would receive a Scorpio car for ₹6 lakh. He appointed Mamta Bhati as a director of the fake company. Promoted heavily on social media, he collected ₹6 lakh each from 250 people, totaling ₹15 crore.
SOG IG Sharad Kaviraj stated that Saini was supposed to deliver the cars by 15 October. Investigation into bank accounts revealed only ₹2.5 lakh, indicating plans to flee, prompting immediate arrests.
Arrests made
- Prince Saini alias Banshilal (24), son of Shankaram Mali, Dhoru, Jodhpur
- Mamta Bhati (24), daughter of Choturam Mali, Kalu, Byawar
- Dinesh Bagri (24), son of Omprakash Mali, Merta City, Nagaur
Authorities are investigating further to trace the defrauded amounts and any additional accomplices involved in the scam.
