1040.0,"Deepfake scams crackdown: YouTube deletes 1,000 scam videos with AI-generated celebrity ads - India TV News",India TV News,"Fri, 26 Jan 2024 08:00:00 GMT",https://www.indiatvnews.com/technology/news/deepfake-scams-crackdown-youtube-deletes-1000-scam-videos-with-ai-generated-celebrity-ads-2024-01-26-913817,success_decoder,success,"Deepfake scams crackdown: YouTube deletes 1,000 scam videos with AI-generated celebrity ads - India TV News",Vishal Upadhyay,2024-01-26,"YouTube, owned by Google, has taken down over 1,000 scam ad videos featuring deepfake technology, where AI is used to make it appear as if celebrities like Taylor Swift, Steve Harvey, and Joe Rogan are promoting Medicare scams. These videos, viewed nearly 200 million times, were removed after a 404 Media investigation exposed the advertising ring behind them.
