1138.0,Class 10 student dies by suicide in UP after AI cheating allegation at school - India Today,India Today,"Sat, 27 Dec 2025 08:00:00 GMT",https://www.indiatoday.in/india/uttar-pradesh/story/class-10-student-dies-by-suicide-in-uttar-pradesh-after-ai-cheating-allegation-at-school-father-alleges-humiliation-and-mental-harassment-2842518-2025-12-27,success_decoder,success,Class 10 student dies by suicide in UP after AI cheating allegation at school,Arvind Ojha,2025-12-27,"Class 10 student dies by suicide in UP after AI cheating allegation at school
A 16-year-old student in Greater Noida West allegedly died by suicide after being questioned over suspected AI use during exams. The incident has sparked allegations of mental harassment against school authorities.
A Class 10 student in Uttar Pradesh allegedly died by suicide after being questioned by her school authorities over the suspected use of AI-based tools during a pre-board examination, triggering allegations of mental harassment and abetment against school officials.
The incident occurred in Greater Noida West. Police said the student was confronted by teachers and the school principal after her mobile phone was allegedly found being used to access AI-assisted answers during the examination.
She jumped from the eighth floor of her residential building on the night of December 22. Police confirmed that no suicide note was recovered from the scene. The body was rushed for post-mortem examination after authorities were alerted.
QUESTIONING OVER ALLEGED EXAM MISCONDUCT
According to the police, the student was called in by the school administration after invigilators detected the alleged use of a mobile phone during the pre-board exam. She was questioned by teachers and later by the principal regarding the suspected violation of examination rules.
Shortly after the incident at school, the student allegedly took her own life. The exact sequence of events following the questioning is part of the ongoing investigation.
FATHER ALLEGES HUMILIATION AND MENTAL HARASSMENT
The family claimed the phone was taken unintentionally, and that teachers reprimanded the girl harshly in class.
The student’s father has filed a police complaint, accusing the school principal and teachers of subjecting his daughter to mental harassment and humiliating her in front of others.
He alleged that the manner in which she was confronted caused severe emotional distress, leaving her traumatised. The complaint accuses the school authorities of abetment to suicide, claiming the pressure and public reprimand pushed the teenager into extreme stress.
SCHOOL DENIES WRONGDOING
The school administration has rejected the allegations. Principal Parul Sardana said the claims were baseless and denied that any student was mentally harassed.
In its version to the police, the school said the student’s phone was confiscated in line with CBSE examination rules and that she was reprimanded strictly but appropriately.
The principal maintained that the interaction was brief, professional and non-abusive, and denied claims that the student was humiliated or verbally mistreated.
CCTV FOOTAGE HANDED OVER, PROBE UNDERWAY
Police said the school has provided CCTV footage related to the incident, which is being examined as part of the investigation. Statements of teachers, school staff and students are also being recorded to establish the circumstances surrounding the questioning and the events that followed.
Officials said further action will depend on the findings of the probe, including whether the questioning crossed permissible disciplinary boundaries.",469,,True,False
