Believing he was speaking directly to the Chief Minister, he transferred ₹80,000 in phased installments to the scammers. Realizing he had been duped after the fraudsters cut the call immediately after the transfer of amount, Reddy approached the Visakhapatnam Cyber Crime Police, who have since registered a case and initiated an investigation.
The incident has once again highlighted the need for awareness among rural people about the ways how cyber criminals are exploiting innocent people and scamming money. Earlier, they used send links and swindle money. But, they are now weaponizing AI deepfakes and voice cloning to impersonate the highest authorities of the state. Even CM is not immune to impersonation.
