Delhi Chief Minister Arvind Kejriwal on Saturday sent the Vigilance Department's report against the Chief Secretary in connection with a 'hospital scam' to Lieutenant Governor VK Saxena.
Kejriwal also demanded theÂ removal of the Delhi Chief Secretary,Â Naresh Kumar, after allegations of the latter's involvement in the scam.
The Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) government has accused Delhi Chief Secretary Naresh Kumar of using his position to secure an artificial intelligence (AI) software development contract for his son's company, MetaMix, with the Institute of Liver and Biliary Sciences (ILBS) Hospital.
According to the report, Naresh Kumar's son's company was allegedly awarded the contract without a tender process.
The company, which is said to have been established only eight months prior to the signing of the memorandum of understanding (MoU) with ILBS, lacks experience in the virtual reality domain, further intensifying suspicions of undue favoritism, as per the Vigilance Department's report.
The Delhi government had earlier accused Kumar of Rs 850 crore land compensation scam linked to the Dwarka Expressway project.
