A major examination scam has come to light at Hemchandracharya North Gujarat University (HNGU). AAP leader Yuvrajsinh Jadeja has exposed malpractices at the Experimental College of Education in Prantij. Students used Artificial Intelligence (AI) on mobile phones to write answers during the examination.
Yuvrajsinh has 24 video evidences. These videos show that the institution's administrators and management provide study materials to students for the examination. Individuals named Ashwin Patel and Sanjay Patel had sent papers to students in advance through WhatsApp.
Appeal to stop the journey from copying to fake Yuvrajsinh stated that due to copying and malpractices, ""fake"" doctors and professors are being produced, which is dangerous for society. He has appealed for immediate steps to be taken to stop these malpractices.
Questions raised on examination of 800 colleges Regarding writing answers using AI, according to Yuvrajsinh, examinations are conducted in this same manner in 800 colleges of HNGU. Despite knowing all this, university officials turn a blind eye. Many colleges violate UGC rules. Colleges are run in complexes, and fees are collected against regulations. Students' original documents are also confiscated.
Demand to release CCTV footage Yuvrajsinh has demanded that police action should be taken against the college in Prantij. He has also demanded to release of CCTV footage and information about MCE examination centers.
Allegations of malpractice during examination Yuvrajsinh Jadeja stated that many instances of copying and malpractice have come to light during M.Sc Semester-4 examinations. Use of mobile and WhatsApp: Question papers are sent in WhatsApp groups, and students are guided to find answers from books.
Institution's support: The institution's management provides students with material (books) for copying.
Cheating captured on CCTV: Yuvrajsinh has released 24 videos that clearly show instances of cheating during the examination.
Allegations against management Yuvrajsinh has accused the institution's administrators, Sanjay Patel and Ashwinkumar Bhikhabhai Patel of assisting in cheating. He stated that these administrators provide all kinds of help to students for copying during exams.
