Visakhapatnam: In yet another shocking case of ""digital arrest"" fraud, cybercriminals posing as Supreme Court authorities duped a 76-year-old man from Vizag of nearly Rs 90 lakh.The victim received calls from individuals claiming to be officials of the apex court in Delhi. They sent fabricated documents via instant messaging, falsely alleging his involvement in unlawful activities and insisting that a petition had been filed against him in the Supreme Court.Despite his denial, the callers maintained that an investigation was underway. Soon after, another fraudster appeared on a video call, impersonating a CBI officer, and declared that the man was under ""digital arrest.""Exploiting his fear, the scammers threatened him with an arrest warrant and demanded transfers to multiple bank accounts for ""verification."" Terrified, the elderly man transferred nearly â¹90 lakh into three SBI accounts.After receiving the money, the fraudsters cut off contact. Days later, they resurfaced, again posing as CBI officers, sending false documents and harassing him for more funds. This time, the victim refused and approached Vizag cybercrime police.
