""When it comes to gangster Lawrence, the accused claim the account in question is being used to park money. The accused then share that they have the photo, address, and other social media-driven details of the victim, which reportedly helps them issue threats and demand ransom.Kolkata Police have issued a fresh advisory for senior citizens, based on the questioning of two persons from Mumbai accused of cheating a 65-year-old of Rs 66.3 lakh last year. Cops have identified at least two dozen Skype IDs with Mumbai Police written on them that were used to carry out the fraud. Since June this year, the Kolkata Police received 320 such complaints.""Sometimes, the scamsters reveal themselves during video calls while at other times, they remain hidden, relying solely on audio using IVR. You must try to hang up, saying you want a written document, not a VOIP call on WhatsApp or Skype. Then verify,"" a joint CP said.Cops analysed over 100 conversations and found a pattern, which they have asked senior citizens to check for. ""The crooks will throw up improbable numbers, and bring in multiple uniformed men on screen, apparently across multiple locations, just to prove the âseriousness of the crime',"" an officer said.
