2348.0,STA Crypto-Ponzi scam: Bureau of Immigration issues look out circular against Hungarian national for deceiving investors - ANI News,ANI News,"Sun, 20 Aug 2023 07:00:00 GMT",https://www.aninews.in/news/national/general-news/sta-crypto-ponzi-scam-bureau-of-immigration-issues-look-out-circular-against-hungarian-national-for-deceiving-investors20230820051214,success_decoder,success,STA Crypto-Ponzi scam: Bureau of Immigration issues look out circular against Hungarian national for deceiving investors,ANI,2026-08-30,"Bhubaneswar (Odisha) [India], August 20 (ANI): The Bureau of Immigration (BOI) has issued a look-out circular (LoC) against a Hungarian national and head of a crypto-Ponzi firm who is allegedly involved in deceiving investors of their money.
32-year-old David Gez, a Hungarian national is the head of a mega Crypto-Ponzi scam namely STA Token.
The firm, STA Token is accused of operating a Ponzi business and collecting around Rs 1,000 crore deposits from two lakh people across the country without any authorisation from the Reserve Bank of India, it said.
Gez entered India twice in 2022-23 on a tourist visa and stayed in India for about 25 days travelling to various places like Odisha, Goa, Punjab, Jharkhand and Delhi, the EOW said.
The first time he had travelled to India via USA and Turkiye and the second time via Poland. In Odisha, he travelled to Bhubaneswar and Bhadrak.
