Woman Held in Fake Marks Card Scam
The arrested has been identified as Safiya Banu (25), a resident of Arakere, Bannerghatta Road.
BENGALURU: Central Crime Branch (CCB) sleuths unearthed an illegal study centre-cum-college which was issuing fake certificates of several universities. A woman has also been arrested in this connection.
The kingpin Raviraj, a native of Secunderabad, is absconding.
Police said the duo was running an educational institution named ‘Vijetha College’ in a 10x10 feet room in Jayanagar 4th Block. Safiya and Raviraj targeted employees of private firms who wanted education certificates and marks cards. The duo used to demand Rs 30,000 to Rs 50,000 to provide marks cards, convocation certificates, post-graduation and doctorate certificates of various universities. The aspirants were asked to take up an examination and had to write it in the building.
The accused was providing fake certificates of Northwest Accreditation Commission, USA (SERI), Madurai Kamaraj University, Dravidian University, Kuppam, Rashtriya Vishwa Vidyapeeth (Mumbai), C V Raman University of Chhattishgarh, Board of Open Distance learning of West Bengal, Global Open University, Nagaland and RKDF University, Kerala.
The students would get marks cards, convocation certificates and even PhD certificates within 30 days of writing the examination. The certificates would be dated back six to seven years to avoid suspicion.
They accused have issued certificates for BA, BCom, BSc, BBM, LSc, MSc, MCom, MBA, MCA, LLM, MA and many other courses.
