MUMBAI: A retired hotel management professional from Andheri (West) fell victim to a sophisticated online scam when he was enticed into investing Rs62,500 after encountering a deepfake video on YouTube featuring Mukesh Ambani endorsing a stock market forum and providing investment advice. Amboli police registered the case based on the complaint filed by PS Jerome (77) on July 9 after he discovered that he was deceived when he stumbled upon the clip on June 14, created using advanced artificial voice cloning technology, which showcases Ambani promoting the forum.This marks the third such incident that has emerged since March, where fraudsters have exploited the chairman and managing director of Reliance Industries' deepfake clip to lure unsuspecting individuals into investing in the stock market, resulting in financial losses for the victims. ""The cyber team is tracking the internet protocol (IP) address and the origin of the clip from where it was uploaded to apprehend the perpetrators. We have requested details of the Moradabad bank account to which the fraudster coerced Jerome to transfer the funds,"" said a police officer from the Amboli police station.Jerome was swindled between June 15 and 18 when he made two fund transfers of Rs12500 and Rs50000 from the savings he had accumulated from the interest he received from his retirement fund. 
