KOLKATA: An 80-year-old resident of Rash Behari Avenue, close to Gariahat, fell victim to yet another digital arrest fraud, losing Rs 33 lakh over a two-week period. The first calls came in mid-June. The incidentinvolved three individuals posing as officers from the Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI).The fraudsters, identified as Ankit Verma, Bijoy Paul, and Amit Kumar, managed to convince the elderly man that he was ""digitally arrested"", a term that played on his fears and lack of familiarity with digital processes. Overwhelmed by the situation and fearing legal repercussions, the victim transferred the money through RTGS to accounts specified by the fraudsters. The case, registered under Gariahat Police Station under sections 318(4), 319(2), and 61(2) of the BNS, is being probed by the cyber cell of the south-east division and Gariahat Police jointly.The police have so far managed to recover Rs 8 lakh. ""The police are continuing their efforts to trace and recover the remaining amount, and we have some leads whereby we are trying to nab the accused and not just restrict ourselves to the recovery. 
