A fake website resembling the Supreme Court's official portal, forged court orders and a network of shell companies were allegedly used to run hundreds of ""digital arrest"" scams across India, the Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) said on Thursday, June 25, after conducting searches at more than 80 locations across 16 states and arresting two people.
The searches, carried out under Operation Chakra-VI by 60 special teams, are part of an investigation into an organised network allegedly linked to more than 200 digital arrest scam cases. Investigators said the accused incorporated shell companies and operated mule bank accounts that were used to launder nearly ₹2 crore in suspected proceeds of crime.
