The Centre is likely to introduce a new law in the ongoing Monsoon Session of Parliament that would make AI-generated deepfakes and ‘digital arrest’ scams separate criminal offences, marking India’s biggest legal overhaul to tackle emerging cybercrimes powered by artificial intelligence.
The move comes after a three-judge bench of the Supreme Court, headed by CJI Surya Kant, and Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohanthe, observed on Tuesday that existing criminal laws do not specifically define either offence, making prosecution and enforcement more difficult. The proposed legislation aims to plug that legal gap by creating dedicated offences with clearly defined punishments.
