A 78-year-old retired Army engineer from Bathinda allegedly lost Rs 35 lakh after fraudsters posing as Delhi Police and Anti-Terrorism Squad (ATS) officials used the digital arrest scam to coerce him into transferring the money.
According to a complaint lodged at the Cyber Crime police station, Ashok Kumar, a resident of Sarabha Nagar in Bathinda, received a phone call on July 13 from an unknown number. The caller claimed to be from the Delhi police headquarters and later connected him to another person who identified himself as an ATS officer.
