4361.0,CBI launches fresh probe into mule accounts linked to digital arrest scams - The Hindu,The Hindu,"Fri, 30 Jan 2026 08:00:00 GMT",https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/cbi-launches-fresh-probe-into-mule-accounts-linked-to-digital-arrest-scams/article70565461.ece,success_decoder,success,CBI launches fresh probe into mule accounts linked to digital arrest scams,The Hindu Bureau,2026-01-30,"The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) has launched a fresh probe to identify those behind several mule accounts that were widely used to divert funds defrauded through major digital arrest scams in Kerala. Some residents of Kozhikode, who allegedly exchanged their bank accounts with anonymous persons in return for commission, have now come under the scanner as part of the intensified investigation.
The police sources said the renewed CBI probe followed the intervention of the Kerala High Court based on complaints filed by a few victims of multi-crore frauds. As part of the exercise, some suspects from rural areas of Kozhikode district have already been questioned by CBI team to make progress in the case.
Preliminary investigations by the local police and special investigation teams revealed that most mule account holders were youngsters seeking passive income. A few college students were also reportedly found to have received a share of the defrauded money as commission for assisting the fraudsters’ operations.
“The details of persons already arrested in connection with various digital scams have been shared with multiple agencies as part of the nationwide probe. This exchange of information has helped agencies uncover the nexus among agents operating within the fraud network,” said a senior officer from the cybercrime investigation wing. He added that some individuals had handed over their bank accounts to strangers without realising they were facilitating digital fraud.
In Kozhikode district, a majority of the identified mule accounts were linked to residents of Kuttiyadi, Perambra and Koyilandy. Over 10 suspected account holders have been arrested over the past year from various rural pockets of the district.
One of the latest findings, according to police sources, is the role of unaccounted money holders in operating mule accounts. The Kozhikode city and rural police have already accessed the bank transaction details of such suspected persons to proceed with a comprehensive probe.
Last year, flash inspections carried out by the CBI under Operation Chakara exposed several intermediaries allegedly colluding with inter-State cybercrime scammers. The seizure of incriminating materials — including KYC documents, mobile phones, bank records and transaction details — seized during those raids enabled the squads to make further headway in the investigation.
